    "title": "'Jeopardy!' Host Has One Regret About His 74-Game Winning Streak",
    "text": "Ken Jennings knows a lot about everything. Well, almost everything, because when it comes to his wardrobe choices during his incredible Jeopardy! run, all he can do now is cringe.The 51-year-old Jeopardy! host and winner of The Greatest Jeopardy! Contestant of All Time took a trip down memory lane and threw a fit about the clothing choices he made during his unparalleled 2004 run that resulted in a 74-game winning streak.Jennings, at the time a software engineer out of Salt Lake City, Utah, opted for a wardrobe that included variety. Instead, he looked like a contestant who wore $3 ties, \"and it really shows.\"The lovable host clowned himself in critiquing his first outfit: a color of shirt \"I would never wear,\" paired with a tie featuring what looks like a bunch of Coca-Cola bottles.\"If I'm seeing that right, that's a terrible tie,\" he quips in a video shared on the game show's Instagram account. \"And, really, it's a color of shirt I would never wear again.\"Jennings admits he was a frugal shopper. He clowned on a tie he says he probably bought in South Korea when he used to live there.\"You could get knockoff clothes for cheap,” Jennings said. “I bet no tie here costs more than, say, $3 American. And it really shows.”In summary, Jennings admits his look resembled that of “some kid wearing his dad’s clothes.” He admits he aimed \"to vary as much as possible\" because he didn't want to wear the same six shirts; otherwise, \"the audience will catch on to that.\"In his defense, no one could have predicted his remarkable run during season 20 of Jeopardy! His streak began on June 2, 2004, and it came to an end on Nov. 30, 2004.In that run, Jennings would go on to win a whopping $2,520,700. He'd make numerous appearances after that before cementing his name in 2020 as The Greatest Jeopardy! Contestant of All Time in a clash against fellow legends Brad Rutter and James Holzhauer.Jennings guest-hosted Jeopardy! following Alex Trebek's death in 2020. He'd later go on to become one of two hosts alongside Mayim Bialik, before earning the full-time role in 2023 ... notably wearing a much more expensive wardrobe.This story was originally reported by Men's Journal on Sep 25, 2025, where it first appeared in the Entertainment section. Add Men's Journal as a Preferred Source by clicking here.",
